# Binary test fixtures must survive checkout byte for byte.
#
# Windows runners default to core.autocrlf=true: anything git considers TEXT
# gets its line endings converted on checkout.  A golden .ppm has no NUL
# bytes in its early pixel data, so git heuristics called it text and the
# conversion shifted every raster by one byte -- the windows CI golden tests
# compared corrupted rasters.  Fuzz corpus inputs are raw bytes with
# meaningful CR/LF sequences and must not be rewritten either.
*.ppm binary
*.webm binary
*.mp4 binary
*.avif binary
tests/fuzz/corpus/** binary
